Step 18 — Cost-Based Dynamic SDN Routing
Goal

Currently Ryu effectively does:

$$ \text{Best Path}=\text{Shortest Path} $$

Both routes have two links:

Path A: s1 → s2 → s4
Path B: s1 → s3 → s4

So hop count alone cannot distinguish them.

After Step 18, we want:

$$ \boxed{\text{Best Path}=\arg\min_P\sum_{e\in P}Cost(e)} $$

For this step, we'll first prove that NetworkX + our Step-17 QoS cost correctly changes the selected path when network conditions change.

We will not yet rewrite the big Ryu controller. This avoids breaking Steps 1–17 before we've validated the routing logic.

