What Step 18 proves

This is a major change from the original project.

Old routing
Network topology
       ↓
Hop count
       ↓
Shortest path
       ↓
OpenFlow

Both:

s1 → s2 → s4

and

s1 → s3 → s4

have two hops.

The controller therefore has no meaningful QoS basis for choosing one.

New routing logic
Delay ──────────┐
Jitter ─────────┤
Loss ───────────┼──→ Normalize
Utilization ────┘        ↓
                    Weighted Cost
                         ↓
                    Link Weight
                         ↓
                NetworkX Dijkstra
                         ↓
                Minimum-Cost Path

